-- title:
--   Lemma 6.7 — residue covering: $kA\equiv Z\pmod\Lambda$ when $\lfloor k/2\rfloor|A\bmod\Lambda|\ge\det\Lambda/\det Z$
-- statement:
--   Let $Z\subseteq\mathbb Z^d$ be a full-dimensional lattice, $\Lambda\subseteq Z$ a full-rank lattice, $A\subseteq Z$ and $k$ an integer. Suppose that
--
--   1. $0\in A\bmod\Lambda$;
--   2. $\lfloor k/2\rfloor\,|A\bmod\Lambda|\ \ge\ \det(\Lambda)/\det(Z)$;
--   3. $|A\bmod\Lambda'|\ge2$ for every proper sublattice $\Lambda'\subsetneq Z$.
--
--   Then $kA\equiv Z\pmod\Lambda$, that is,
--   $$kA\bmod\Lambda=Z\bmod\Lambda,$$
--   where $kA$ is the $k$-fold sumset of $A$.
--
--   This is the covering step of Theorem 1.3: enough copies of $A$ reach every residue class of $Z$ modulo the lattice generated by a barycentric spanner.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Determinants are indices in $\mathbb Z^d$. In condition 3 the number of residues is counted in $\mathbb N\cup\{\infty\}$, since $\mathbb Z^d/\Lambda'$ may be infinite.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a full-rank (full-dimensional) lattice, $\det(\Lambda)$ → an additive subgroup of finite index, $\det$ = its index; reason: the index of a full-rank sublattice of $\mathbb Z^d$ equals the absolute determinant of any basis; same objects
--   - reading: every proper sublattice $\Lambda'\subsetneq Z$ → every proper additive subgroup $\Lambda'<Z$; reason: every subgroup of $\mathbb Z^d$ is a lattice; requiring condition 3 only for full-rank proper sublattices is equivalent, since a coset of a lower-rank $\Lambda'$ lies in a coset of the full-rank proper $\Lambda'+2Z$
-- source:
--   Lin Chen, Tingwei Hu, Jiayi Lian, Yuchen Mao, Guochuan Zhang, Faster Approximation Schemes for Scheduling on Related Machines, STOC 2027 submission #796 (October 2026), source.pdf SHA-256 5d7d0135eed9cbe942c80598e2bb07d8c56ab67aec0d6e8486a067237654f7f3, p.20, Lemma 6.7 (proof pp.20–21, including Claim 6.8)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RelatedSchedFPTAS796_Main_Lattice

set_option autoImplicit false

open Pointwise

namespace RelatedSchedFPTAS796.Main

/-- **Lemma 6.7**, p.20 (proof pp.20–21). Let `Z ⊆ ℤ^d` be a full-dimensional lattice,
`Λ ⊆ Z` a full-rank lattice, `A ⊆ Z`, and `k` an integer. Suppose (1) `0 ∈ A mod Λ`;
(2) `⌊k/2⌋·|A mod Λ| ≥ det(Λ)/det(Z)`; (3) `|A mod Λ'| ≥ 2` for every proper sublattice
`Λ' ⊊ Z`. Then `kA ≡ Z (mod Λ)`, i.e. `kA mod Λ = Z mod Λ`. Determinants are indices in `ℤ^d`;
`|A mod Λ'|` is counted in `ℕ∞` since `ℤ^d/Λ'` may be infinite. -/
theorem lemma_6_7 {d : ℕ} (Z Λ : AddSubgroup (Fin d → ℤ)) (hZ : Z.FiniteIndex)
    (hΛ : Λ.FiniteIndex) (hΛZ : Λ ≤ Z) (A : Set (Fin d → ℤ)) (hAZ : A ⊆ Z) (k : ℕ)
    (h1 : (0 : (Fin d → ℤ) ⧸ Λ) ∈ modL Λ A)
    (h2 : (Λ.index : ℚ) / Z.index ≤ ((k / 2 : ℕ) : ℚ) * Nat.card (modL Λ A))
    (h3 : ∀ Λ' : AddSubgroup (Fin d → ℤ), Λ' < Z → 2 ≤ (modL Λ' A).encard) :
    modL Λ (k • A) = modL Λ (Z : Set (Fin d → ℤ)) := by sorry

end RelatedSchedFPTAS796.Main
